{ns}
{define: CaddD base-fret 1 frets x 3 2 0 3 0} 
{define: CaddG base-fret 1 frets x 3 2 0 1 3} 
{define: E7 base-fret 1 frets 0 2 0 1 0 0} 
{define: Esus4 base-fret 1 frets 0 0 2 2 0 0} 
{define: G6 base-fret 1 frets 3 2 0 0 0 0} 
{t: WITHOUT YOU – Harry Nilsson }
{st: (Evans/Ham) }
{artist: Harry Nilsson }
{composer: Evans; Ham }


https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8dnUv3DUP4E  (Capo 4) (MC1/2)

TIP:  For the piano intro, (CaddD) is just (C) with your pinky added to note <d> at the 2nd string/3rd fret).  So form up (CaddD) and it’s just on/off while holding the (C) shape.

TIP:  The first line of each verse has a variation of (Esus4).  Think of this as (Am) without the index finger, or an (Em) shape but one string lower.  

TIP:  At the end of the first chorus Harry drops his voice on the trailing “more” to hit note <f> so just lift off your index finger from the trailing (G7) to arrive at (G6).  Strum once.  At the beginning of the next verse there’s another (CaddD).  If this is cumbersome to hit, just play (C) straight through to the (Em) on “face.”

TIP:  At the beginning of the last chorus Harry hits a high <g> so play (CaddG) here which is just (C) with your pinky added to the 1st string/3rd fret.  Similar to (CaddD) but one string higher.
          

